Stephen Ramsay wrote:
> I've been playing nethack for a couple of years.  I have played mostly the
> Valk, though I have recently started playing the Samurai more and more.

The valkyrie is an appropriate choice to start with.

> Problem is, I just can't break the sixth or seventh level, and I feel like I'm
> doing something fundamentally wrong.

Hard to tell what you are doing wrong since you say that you read all
howtos.  What is the primary death reason in your case?  Analyze the
log file and try to avoid these deaths.  If for example you are killed
by hordes, retreat into some alleyway to handle them one by one.  Try to
keep your pet help you in combat.  Avoid the mines, they are wide open
area, you will have difficulties to defend yourself.  Write Elbereth in
the dust when you are in distress.  Pray - but not too often - if you
are at 5 HP or below.

> I know lots of tricks, and my character has usually got (what I think is) a
> decent armour class by the time I get down to six (1,0, or -1 usually).  I also
> usually have a Skilled rating in long sword (katana).  I have my share of
> stupid and/or random deaths, but I mostly just get cornered and clobbered on
> the sixth or seventh level.

That AC is far from excellent.  Some monsters kick really hard (mumak)
or make lot of damage (soldier ant).  Avoid these and retreat, flee!
Use ranged attacks, identify wands as soon as possible to help you.

> I've read all the beginner's guides I can find, and I think I've groked what
> they have to say, but I just can't get any further.

Again, analyze what you are doing in fatal situations and try to find
different solutions.  Don't type too fast.  Sit back and think of a
situation that might most likely become a problem.  Remember, instant
deaths are not that often, most problems can somehow be avoided.
If you have a problem, stop playing and ask this newsgroup about the
concrete problem.

> Anyone have any advice for a stuck warrior?  What experience level are people
> usually at when they get down to six or seven?

Your task is *not* to descend as fast as possible.  And the level is
not that important (IMO).  You must have a safe feeling about that you
can handle the all the monsters that usually appear within some level
range.  And you must be prepared that there *always* might appear some
unexpected hard monster or difficult situation where you have to think
about a solution.  Often enough, there is no guaranteed solution, and
the question is simply: Will you or the creature lose his last HP first?

It's typical for nethack that there is no strict schema or behaviour
how to handle all problematic situations.  If you have some concrete
problem come in and ask, you're welcome.

